# Project: Patient Triage Assistant -- Agentic AI Webinar Demo

## What This Project Is

A 45-minute webinar demo showcasing agentic AI in healthcare using an open-source stack. The deliverable is a **Patient Triage Assistant** that helps triage nurses during patient intake: looking up patient records, assessing symptom urgency, checking drug interactions, and booking specialist appointments.

This is a **demo application** with self-contained mock data. MCP servers use in-memory sample data, not real hospital backends.

## Architecture: Llama Stack as Full Middleware

The central architectural decision: **Llama Stack (OGX) is the full AI middleware**, not just a model router. It handles:
1. **Model routing** -- inference routed to vLLM backends via `remote::vllm` provider
2. **MCP tool execution** -- MCP servers registered as connectors, executed server-side
3. **Agentic orchestration** -- the full inference -> tool_call -> execute -> re-inference loop runs inside Llama Stack via `/v1/responses`

The Quarkus application is a **thin chat UI**. It calls Llama Stack's `/v1/responses` endpoint and renders the response. It does NOT contain MCP client logic, LangChain4j, or agentic loop management.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| Chat UI | Quarkus + WebSockets + REST Client | Thin UI, sends requests to Llama Stack `/v1/responses` |
| AI Middleware | Llama Stack (OGX) via Operator | Model routing, MCP connectors, server-side agentic loop |
| Model Serving | OpenShift AI 3.4 + vLLM | On-premise LLM hosting (Mistral Small 3.1 24B INT4 via ModelCar) |
| Agent Tools | 3x Quarkus MCP Servers (Streamable HTTP) | Patient records, medical knowledge, scheduling |
| Platform | OpenShift 4.16+ | Container orchestration |

